NAME
    info — Display detailed information about a file or directory.

SYNOPSIS
    info <path>

DESCRIPTION
    The 'info' command displays useful information about a file or directory.
    It shows the path, type, size, permissions, modification date, and creation
    date.

    Basically, it asks your file: "So... tell me about yourself."

ARGUMENTS
    path    The file or directory to inspect.
    Can be relative or absolute.

EXAMPLES
    > info myfile.txt
        Displays detailed information about myfile.txt.

    > info documents
        Displays information about the documents directory.

    > info /home/user/file.txt
        Displays information about a file using its absolute path.

OUTPUT
    Path         The complete path of the file or directory.
    Type         File or Directory.
    Size         The size of the file in a human-readable format.
    Permissions  The file permissions.
    Modified     The date and time when the item was last modified.
    Created      The creation date and time of the item.

FUN FACTS
    - Directories have a size too. Yes, even empty ones.
    - Permissions tell you who can do what with the file.
    - Modified and Created are not necessarily the same date.
    - info is basically the file manager version of asking "Who are you?"

